verview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into the SAP BTP community, focusing on key components and their interactions within the organizational framework. The information is relevant to the community's operations around 2024.\n\n## SAP BTP Command Line Interface Operational Scope\n\nThe SAP BTP Command Line Interface plays a pivotal role in managing SAP BTP services. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential operational pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective management not only prevents operational anomalies but also supports the community's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (123, 1771), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 12))]\n\n## SAP Document AI and Governance\n\nSAP Document AI ensures that all SAP BTP operations adhere to the technological standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on document processing and AI, noted starting 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex documents and AI agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high technological standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (2145), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 12))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between SAP BTP components, established in 2024, ensures that operational strategies are technologically sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP BTP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the community's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (1772, 1773), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 12))]", "# SAP Technology and Intelligent Technologies Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key departments focusing on technology and intelligent technologies, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to drive innovation and operational efficiency. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2024.\n\n## Cloud Foundry and Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nCloud Foundry and Kyma Runtime have been updated with new features and enhancements, including improved security, scalability, and performance. These updates aim to provide a more robust and efficient platform for SAP's customers and developers. [Data: Sources (1772, 3557), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 12))]\n\n## SAP Document AI Enhancements\n\nSAP Document AI has been enhanced with new features and capabilities, including improved machine learning models, instant learning, and list of values data type. These enhancements aim to provide better document information extraction, processing, and analysis for SAP's customers. [Data: Sources (3552, 3554), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 05), (2024, 12, 12))]\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Updates\n\nSAP Build Process Automation has been updated with new features and capabilities, including advanced functions for decisions, flattening object structure, and update task attributes in batch. These updates aim to provide a more efficient and intuitive user experience for SAP's customers and developers. [Data: Sources (3559, 2026), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 02), (2024, 12, 12))]\n\n## SAP HANA Service Updates\n\nSAP HANA Service has been updated with new features and capabilities, including improved performance, scalability, and security. These updates aim to provide a more robust and efficient platform for SAP's customers and developers. [Data: Sources (377, 1368), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 20), (2025, 02, 20))]\n\n## SAP Java Buildpack Updates\n\nSAP Java Buildpack has been updated with new features and capabilities, including improved performance, scalability, and security. These updates aim to provide a more robust and efficient platform for SAP's customers and developers. [Data: Sources (1370), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 05), (2025, 02, 20))]", "# SAP Joule and BTP Overview as of April 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key components focusing on Joule and BTP, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide innovative solutions and services. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around mid-2025.\n\n## Joule's Capabilities and Features\n\nJoule is a conversational AI that helps platform administrators ask questions related to their BTP resources, such as users or the runtime environment, in the cockpit. It provides information about global accounts or subaccounts, users, and permissions, and assists with administrative tasks related to Cloud Foundry. Joule's capabilities are essential for holistic governance and have been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (66, 68, 1106), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2025, 04, 30))]\n\n## Joule's Multi-Language Support\n\nJoule now supports multiple languages, ensuring users experience Joule in their desired language, providing localized messages, product data, and more. It automatically adopts the language configured within the SAP application, and can understand languages other than those officially supported. This feature is crucial for SAP's global operations, allowing users to interact with Joule in their native language. [Data: Sources (67, 1107), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2025, 04, 30))]\n\n## BTP's General Availability\n\nBTP's general availability is currently being rolled out in stages to global accounts during the second quarter of 2025. Joule's general availability is also being rolled out in stages to global accounts during the same period. This rollout is essential for SAP's global operations, ensuring that users have access to the latest features and capabilities. [Data: Sources (68, 1106), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2025, 04, 30))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significant updates as of 2025. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's operations and development.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Environment\n\nCloud Foundry is a key environment within SAP BTP, supporting various components such as SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition, and Pricing Service. Its updates and improvements are essential for the platform's overall performance and functionality. [Data: Sources (1, 2, 3), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 08, 14))]\n\n## Pricing Service Updates\n\nThe Pricing Service has undergone significant updates, including the correction of condition base calculation issues and validation fixes for zero-value conditions. These improvements are crucial for ensuring accurate pricing and preventing potential errors. [Data: Sources (4, 5, 6), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 25), (2025, 07, 09))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Enhancements\n\nKyma Runtime has received enhancements, including the release of the Cloud Manager module and updates to the Telemetry module. These improvements are essential for maintaining the platform's stability and security. [Data: Sources (7, 8, 9), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 20), (2025, 07, 09))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of August 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their core attributes, connections, and noteworthy claims. The information is relevant to SAP's technology landscape around August 2025.\n\n## SAP Build Work Zone, Advanced Edition\n\nSAP Build Work Zone, Advanced Edition, is a powerful tool that enables users to create custom applications and workflows. Its integration with document grounding allows for the use of company-specific content as a source for AI queries, providing valuable business-related context. This feature is essential for companies looking to leverage AI and machine learning in their operations. [Data: Sources (309, 310), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 13), (2025, 08, 13))]\n\n## SAP Task Center\n\nThe SAP Task Center is a web application that allows users to view their task history with the Activity Log. This feature is crucial for tracking and managing tasks, ensuring that users stay on top of their work and meet deadlines. The SAP Task Center is an essential tool for companies looking to improve their project management and productivity. [Data: Source (301), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 14), (2025, 08, 14))]\n\n## ABAP Environment\n\nThe ABAP Environment is a platform that enables developers to create and deploy custom applications. The ability to publish add-on products as an alternative to the multitenancy SaaS solution is a significant feature, allowing companies to expand their offerings and reach new customers. This feature is essential for companies looking to innovate and stay competitive in the market. [Data: Source (302), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 12), (2025, 08, 13))]\n\n## Cloud Integration\n\nCloud Integration is a service that enables companies to integrate their cloud-based applications and services. The support for Client Certificate-based authentication for JMS Variants is a significant feature, ensuring secure and reliable communication between applications. This feature is essential for companies looking to improve their integration and interoperability. [Data: Source (303), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 13), (2025, 08, 13))]\n\n## Pricing Service\n\nThe Pricing Service is a platform that enables companies to manage their pricing and revenue streams. The support for more standard pricing routines and the ability to determine condition values during repricing are significant features, ensuring accurate and efficient pricing. This feature is essential for companies looking to improve their revenue management and customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (305, 306, 307), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 25), (2025, 08, 13))]\n\n## Responsibility Management Service\n\nThe Responsibility Management Service is a platform that enables companies to manage their responsibilities and tasks. The availability on the Google Cloud Platform in AP30 (Sydney, Australia) is a significant feature, ensuring global reach and scalability. This feature is essential for companies looking to improve their operational efficiency and customer satisfaction. [Data: Source (308), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 13), (2025, 08, 13))]", "# SAP Technology Updates as of August 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of key SAP technology updates, highlighting the integration of various components and services within the SAP ecosystem. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around August 2025.\n\n## SAP Task Center Enhancements\n\nThe SAP Task Center has been enhanced with the Activity Log feature, allowing users to view their task history. This update is part of SAP's efforts to improve user experience and streamline task management. The Activity Log feature is now available in the SAP Task Center Web app, providing users with a clear understanding of their task history and progress. This update is crucial for ensuring that users can effectively manage their tasks and stay on top of their workloads. [Data: Sources (706), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 14), (2025, 08, 14))]\n\n## ABAP Environment Updates\n\nThe ABAP Environment has been updated to support the delivery of add-on products through the Landscape Portal. This update allows partners to publish their products as add-on products, providing customers with a second delivery option. The Landscape Portal is used for both publishing and installing add-on products, making it easier for customers to access and install the products they need. This update is critical for SAP's partner ecosystem, enabling partners to expand their offerings and customers to access a wider range of products. [Data: Sources (302), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 12), (2025, 08, 13))]\n\n## Cloud Integration Updates\n\nThe Cloud Integration service has been updated to support a new version of the IBM MQ adapter, which includes client certificate-based authentication for JMS variants. This update enhances the security and reliability of the Cloud Integration service, ensuring that customers can trust the service to handle their data and integrations. The new version of the IBM MQ adapter also provides improved performance and scalability, making it easier for customers to integrate their applications and services. [Data: Sources (303), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 13), (2025, 08, 13))]\n\n## Pricing Service Updates\n\nThe Pricing Service has been updated to support new pricing requirement formulas and base value formulas. These updates enable customers to take advantage of new pricing options and formulas, making it easier for them to manage their pricing and revenue. The Pricing Service has also been updated to stop writing pricing determination traces when an estimated memory size of about 5MB is reached, improving performance and reducing the risk of errors. [Data: Sources (305, 306, 307), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 25), (2025, 08, 13))]\n\n## Responsibility Management Service Updates\n\nThe Responsibility Management Service is now available on the Google Cloud Platform in AP30 (Sydney, Australia). This update expands the service's availability and provides customers with greater flexibility and choice when it comes to deploying the service. The new data center in AP30 also improves the service's performance and reliability, ensuring that customers can trust the service to handle their data and integrations. [Data: Sources (308), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 13), (2025, 08, 13))]", "# SAP Cloud Services Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's cloud services, highlighting key components, their environments, and recent updates. The information is relevant to SAP's cloud operations as of 2025.\n\n## Cloud Logging and Monitoring\n\nSAP Cloud Logging service is now available on multiple regions, including cf-jp31, cf-eu31, cf-ca20, and cf-ap31. This expansion enhances the service's availability and scalability, allowing customers to better monitor and manage their cloud resources. [Data: Sources (620), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 30), (2025, 06, 30))]\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Enhancements\n\nSAP Build Process Automation, Foundation Add-On by UiPath 2.0 offers several enhancements, including the ability to share feedback and complete surveys while using UiPath automations, improved automation support for SAP applications, and enhanced out-of-band logging capabilities. These updates improve the overall user experience and increase the service's efficiency. [Data: Source (622), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 30), (2025, 06, 30))]\n\n## Cloud Integration for Data Services\n\nSAP Cloud Integration for data services now supports Azure user-assigned and system-assigned managed identities as an authentication method for connecting to Microsoft SQL Server databases hosted as PaaS on Azure and to Gen 2 Azure Data Lake Storage file locations. This update expands the service's capabilities and improves its security features. [Data: Source (626), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 27), (2025, 06, 27))]\n\n## API Management Updates\n\nAPI Management has introduced Predictions, an AI-based capability that identifies trends in API calls and predicts future API traffic. This feature enables customers to optimize resource allocation, manage system load, and make informed decisions about their API strategy. [Data: Source (1452), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 08), (2025, 02, 08))]\n\n## Data Space Integration Updates\n\nData Space Integration has introduced several updates, including contract references, software version updates, and new features. These updates improve the service's functionality and user experience, allowing customers to better manage their data spaces. [Data: Sources (1454, 1455), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 08), (2025, 02, 08))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Upgrade\n\nThe Kyma environment is planned to be upgraded to the Kubernetes version 1.31 in the 2025 Q1 Maintenance and Major Upgrade Window. This upgrade will improve the service's performance, security, and scalability, allowing customers to better manage their cloud resources. [Data: Source (1458), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 08), (2025, 01, 08))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of February 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their operational scope, connections, and noteworthy updates. The information is relevant to SAP's technology landscape around February 2025.\n\n## API Management Operational Scope\n\nThe API Management Department at SAP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating risks associated with API calls. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential technological pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective API management not only prevents technological anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (2, 3), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 02, 08))]\n\n## Data Space Integration and Governance\n\nThe Data Space Integration Department ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on contract management, noted starting 2025, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (4), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 02, 08))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the API Management and Data Space Integration Departments, established in 2025, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider technological risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (6, 7), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 02, 08))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Upgrade\n\nThe Kyma Runtime environment is planned to be upgraded to the Kubernetes version 1.31 in the 2025 Q1 Maintenance and Major Upgrade Window. This upgrade aims to improve the performance and security of the Kyma environment, ensuring that it remains compatible with the latest technological advancements. The upgrade schedule has been carefully planned to minimize disruptions to SAP's operations. [Data: Source (8), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 08), (2025, 02, 08))]\n\n## Trading Partner Management Enhancements\n\nThe Trading Partner Management Department has enhanced the retry mechanism in integration flow Step 2 - Interchange Processing Flow V2 with an idempotent process call, ensuring that only failed payloads are retried, and minimizing redundant reprocessing of successful payloads. This enhancement aims to improve the efficiency and reliability of SAP's trading partner management processes. [Data: Source (10), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 02, 08))]", "# SAP Technology Updates as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key updates and changes in SAP technology as of 2025, focusing on the components and environments that have undergone significant modifications. The report highlights the importance of these updates in enhancing the functionality and security of SAP systems.\n\n## Generative AI Hub Updates\n\nThe Generative AI hub has undergone significant updates, with the deprecation of GPT-4 versions 0613 and turbo-2024-04-09, as well as gpt-4-32k version 0613. It is recommended that users migrate to GPT-4.1 as a replacement. This update is crucial in ensuring the continued functionality and security of the Generative AI hub. [Data: Sources (441, 442, 443), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 02), (2025, 06, 02))]\n\n## API Management Updates\n\nAPI Management has undergone several updates, including the introduction of new role collections, support for API artifacts in access policies, and improved navigation for onboarding. These updates are essential in enhancing the functionality and security of API Management, ensuring compliance with regulatory standards, and providing users with enhanced features. [Data: Sources (38, 511, 512, 513, 514, 515, 516, 517, 518, 519), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 06), (2025, 07, 06))]\n\n## Data Space Integration Updates\n\nData Space Integration has undergone updates, including the introduction of a custom connector URL and software version updates. These updates are crucial in ensuring the continued functionality and security of Data Space Integration, ensuring compliance with regulatory standards, and providing users with enhanced features. [Data: Sources (195, 514, 515, 516, 517, 518, 519), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 06), (2025, 07, 06))]", "# SAP Cloud Services Overview as of June 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's cloud services, highlighting key components, their environments, and recent updates. The information is relevant to SAP's cloud operations around mid-2025.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP have been upgraded, introducing new features and improvements. The services now support new attribute activationUrl located in the user extension schema urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:sap:2.0:User. This enhancement enables users to activate links for their user accounts, improving user experience and convenience. [Data: Sources (2, 3), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 04), (2025, 06, 04))]\n\n## Generative AI Hub Updates\n\nThe Generative AI hub at SAP has been updated, with several models being deprecated and replaced with newer versions. GPT-4 versions 0613 and turbo-2024-04-09, as well as gpt-4-32k version 0613, have been deprecated and replaced with GPT-4.1. Gemini-1.5-pro and gemini-1.5-flash have been deprecated and replaced with gemini-2.0-flash or gemini-2.0-flash-lite. Mistralai--mixtral08x7b-v01 has been deprecated and replaced with mistralai--mistral-small-instruct. These updates aim to improve the performance and quality of the AI models. [Data: Sources (7, 8, 9), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 02), (2025, 06, 02))]\n\n## API Management Updates\n\nAPI Management at SAP has been updated, introducing new features and improvements. A navigation change has been implemented in the SAP Integration Suite for enabling the Analytics AI features. Additionally, three new granular role collections have been introduced: APIPortal.Configurator, APIPortal.Developer, and APIPortal.Tester. These updates aim to improve the flexibility and control in managing API Management entities. [Data: Sources (17, 18), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 01), (2025, 06, 01))]", "# Catena-X Technology Overview as of May 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of Catena-X's key technology components, highlighting their integration and updates as of May 2025. The information is relevant to the company's technology operations during this period.\n\n## Data Space Integration Updates\n\nCatena-X has updated its Data Space Integration to version 1.8.* as of May 2025. This update includes the Tractus-X Eclipse Dataspace Connector version 0.7.6 and FOSS Eclipse Dataspace Components version 0.7.2. The update is part of the company's efforts to improve its technology infrastructure and support its operations. [Data: Sources (430), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 04), (2025, 05, 04))]\n\n## Integration Advisor Updates\n\nThe Integration Advisor component has been updated to version 1.99.* as of May 2025. This update includes the Mass Validate XSLT Snippets feature, which allows users to mass validate all their XSLT snippets inside their mapping guideline (MAG). The update also includes the Software Version Update, which updates the SAP Integration Advisor to version 1.99.*. [Data: Sources (968, 969), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 04), (2025, 05, 04))]\n\n## Message XSD File Updates\n\nThe Integration Advisor component has also been updated to allow users to choose between the full or reduced message XSD file in their message implementation guideline (MIG) for EDI type systems. This update is part of the company's efforts to improve its technology infrastructure and support its operations. [Data: Source (970), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 04), (2025, 05, 04))]", "# SAP Cloud Integration and Identity Services Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key services focusing on cloud integration and identity services, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide secure and efficient integration solutions. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2025.\n\n## Cloud Integration Operational Scope\n\nSAP Cloud Integration plays a pivotal role in facilitating data exchange between various systems and applications. Its proactive approach, highlighted throughout 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential data exchange pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective cloud integration not only prevents data anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (282, 448, 634), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 09, 25))]\n\n## Identity Services and User Authentication\n\nSAP Identity Services ensures that all user authentication processes adhere to the latest security standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on secure user authentication, noted throughout 2025, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational security, especially in managing complex user access and authentication processes. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high security standards and protecting customer data. [Data: Source (524), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 11), (2025, 09, 25))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Integration\n\nCollaboration between SAP Cloud Integration and Identity Services, established throughout 2025, ensures that integration solutions are secure and efficient. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating cloud integration with identity services strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (282, 448, 634), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 09, 25))]", "# SAP Cloud Integration and Migration Assessment Overview as of July 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP Cloud Integration and Migration Assessment, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2025.\n\n## Migration Assessment Operational Scope\n\nThe Migration Assessment component at SAP Cloud Integration plays a pivotal role in evaluating and recommending migration strategies. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP Cloud Integration against potential integration pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective migration assessment not only prevents integration anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (233, 234), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 07, 27))]\n\n## Trading Partner Management Updates\n\nThe Trading Partner Management component at SAP Cloud Integration has seen significant updates, including the addition of new type systems for B2B transactions and software version updates. These changes aim to enhance the integration process and improve the overall user experience. [Data: Sources (395, 396), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 07, 27))]\n\n## Connectivity Service Updates\n\nThe Connectivity service at SAP Cloud Integration has planned to enable IPv4 and IPv6 dual stack ingress for AWS-based regions. This update aims to improve the connectivity and accessibility of the service. [Data: Source (398), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 07, 27))]\n\n## API Management Integration\n\nThe API Management component at SAP Cloud Integration has been integrated with SAP Cloud ALM for centralized developer hub certificate expiry monitoring. This integration enables proactive certificate management and helps prevent unexpected disruptions. [Data: Source (534), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 07, 27))]\n\n## Data Space Integration Updates\n\nThe Data Space Integration component at SAP Cloud Integration has seen significant updates, including the removal of message queue functionality and software version updates. These changes aim to improve the integration process and enhance the overall user experience. [Data: Sources (382, 383), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 07, 27))]\n\n## Event Mesh Updates\n\nThe Event Mesh component at SAP Cloud Integration has seen significant updates, including the addition of new role collection and message monitoring. These changes aim to improve the overall user experience and enhance the integration process. [Data: Sources (384, 385), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 07, 27))]\n\n## Integration Advisor Updates\n\nThe Integration Advisor component at SAP Cloud Integration has seen significant updates, including the harmonization of user interface for code value mappings and software version updates. These changes aim to improve the overall user experience and enhance the integration process. [Data: Sources (386, 387, 388), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 07, 27))]", "# Cloud Foundry and Kyma Runtime Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into the key components and services of Cloud Foundry and Kyma Runtime, highlighting their interactions and updates within the organizational framework. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2025.\n\n## Cloud Transport Management Updates\n\nCloud Transport Management has introduced several updates, including enhancements to the Create Node dialog, a new function in the import queue, and a revamp of the Landscape Action Logs. These updates aim to simplify the import process, improve automation, and enhance data analysis and audit compliance. The latest revision of Cloud Transport Management is version 2504a, valid as of 2025-05-06 [Data: Sources (1, 2, 3), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 06), (2025, 05, 06))].\n\n## API Gateway Module Updates\n\nThe API Gateway module has undergone several updates, including the introduction of APIRule v2 and the deletion of v1beta1. The latest version of the API Gateway module is 3.0.2, valid as of 2025-05-05 [Data: Sources (4, 5), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 05), (2025, 05, 05))].\n\n## Data Space Integration Updates\n\nData Space Integration has introduced several updates, including the assignment of an assignees column in company policies and software version updates. The latest version of Data Space Integration is 1.8.*, valid as of 2025-05-04 [Data: Sources (6, 7), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 04), (2025, 05, 04))].\n\n## Mobile Services Updates\n\nMobile Services has introduced several updates, including direct links to the SAP BTP Cockpit and Dev Space Manager, a full initial download from the offline service, and the inclusion of predefined annotations. The latest version of Mobile Services is 2503, valid as of 2025-04-10 [Data: Sources (8, 9), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 10), (2025, 04, 10))].\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nKyma Runtime has introduced several updates, including an update to the API Gateway module and a watch mechanism to ensure that DNSEntry is up to date. The latest version of Kyma Runtime is 2.11.3, valid as of 2025-04-09 [Data: Sources (10, 11), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 09), (2025, 04, 09))].", "# SAP Cloud Platform Updates Overview as of 2024-10-30\n\nThis report delves into the key updates and enhancements on the SAP Cloud Platform, focusing on the components and environments that have undergone significant changes. The information is relevant to the platform's operations around mid-2024.\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Enhancements\n\nThe SAP Build Process Automation component has introduced new functions, including ISLOWERCASE and ISUPPERCASE, which can be used in decisions. This enhancement supports more complex decision-making processes and improves the overall efficiency of the platform. The update is part of the platform's continuous effort to provide users with more advanced tools and features [Data: Sources (2026), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 25), (2024, 10, 30))].\n\n## SAP Document AI Improvements\n\nThe SAP Document AI component has undergone significant improvements, including the ability to create and manage schema versions on the basic UI. This feature allows users to adapt existing schemas for similar use cases, reducing the need for manual copying or adaptation. The update also includes improved underlying infrastructure for LLM-usage, enhancing service performance [Data: Sources (2027, 2028), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 25), (2024, 10, 30))].\n\n## API Gateway Module Updates\n\nThe API Gateway module has introduced several updates, including the postponement of the APIRule v2 upgrade and the deletion of v1beta1. The update also includes the release of API Gateway 3.0.2, which introduces APIRule CR in the stable version v2. This feature allows users to expose workloads using one of the three supported access strategies: jwt, noAuth, and extAuth [Data: Sources (2030, 2031, 2032), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 25), (2025, 05, 05))].\n\n## Data Space Integration Updates\n\nThe Data Space Integration component has introduced several updates, including the assignees column available in company policies and software version updates. The update also includes the latest versions of Data Space Integration, Tractus-X Eclipse Dataspace Connector, and FOSS Eclipse Dataspace Components [Data: Sources (2033, 2034), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 25), (2025, 05, 04))].", "# Kyma Runtime and SAP Technology Updates Overview as of June 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of key updates and changes within the Kyma Runtime and SAP technology ecosystem, highlighting the importance of these updates in enhancing the functionality and performance of various components. The information is relevant to the technology landscape as of June 2025.\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nThe Kyma Runtime has undergone several updates, including the Istio module update to version 1.18.0 and the Telemetry module update to version 1.41.0. These updates have unified Istio extensibility views in the Kyma dashboard and improved logging capabilities, respectively. The updates have been made available in the General Availability lifecycle, ensuring that they are stable and secure for use in production environments. [Data: Sources (498, 499), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 29), (2025, 06, 11))]\n\n## SAP HANA Spatial Services Enhancements\n\nSAP HANA Spatial Services has received enhancements, including mapping API, routing API, and geocoding API updates. These updates have improved the performance and security of the service, ensuring that it can handle complex spatial data and provide accurate results. The updates have been made available in the General Availability lifecycle, ensuring that they are stable and secure for use in production environments. [Data: Source (673), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2025, 06, 11))]\n\n## Document Management Service Updates\n\nThe Document Management Service has undergone updates, including the 'maxItems' parameter update in the getChildren and Query API. This update has reduced the default and maximum value for the 'maxItems' parameter to 25,000, enhancing the response time and preventing open-ended parameter values that could potentially impact performance. The update has been made available in the General Availability lifecycle, ensuring that it is stable and secure for use in production environments. [Data: Source (674), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 10), (2025, 06, 10))]\n\n## Cloud Integration Updates\n\nCloud Integration has received several updates, including changes to the General and Iterating Splitter XPath Expression and Grouping, the ability to configure the target root element in EDI to XML Converter, and the option to choose how to process empty files in the SFTP Adapter. These updates have improved the functionality and performance of the service, ensuring that it can handle complex data and provide accurate results. The updates have been made available in the General Availability lifecycle, ensuring that they are stable and secure for use in production environments. [Data: Sources (676, 677, 678), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 07), (2025, 06, 07))]\n\n## SAP Document AI Updates\n\nSAP Document AI has received updates, including the configuration API and a new improved ML model for purchase order documents. These updates have improved the performance and security of the service, ensuring that it can handle complex data and provide accurate results. The updates have been made available in the General Availability lifecycle, ensuring that they are stable and secure for use in production environments. [Data: Sources (779, 780), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 27), (2025, 05, 27))]"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_68ffbc0fd0baae8796161c139c9db333e8c70c7b03d867d7751637bb5733e4db_v2"}